---
import LegalPage from '@/components/LegalPage.astro';
import { legalHolder as h } from '@/lib/data';
---

<LegalPage title="Legal Notice" description="Legal notice for the portfolio of Pablo Blázquez Gil — Photography and Filmmaking.">
  <p>
    This English version is provided for convenience. In the event of any discrepancy, the <a href="/aviso-legal" hreflang="es">Spanish version</a> shall prevail. Last updated: {h.updated.en}.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>1. Website owner</h2>
    <p>In accordance with article 10 of Spanish Law 34/2002 on Information Society Services and Electronic Commerce (LSSI), the owner of this website is:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Owner: <strong>{h.name}</strong></li>
      <li>Tax ID (NIF): {h.nif}</li>
      <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${h.email}`}>{h.email}</a></li>
      <li>Activity: professional photography and video</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>2. Purpose</h2>
    <p>This website presents the photography and video work of {h.name} and serves as a contact channel. Its content is for information only and is not a contractual offer: services are hired through a specific quote or contract.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>3. Intellectual and industrial property</h2>
    <p>The photographs, videos, texts, design and other content of this website are the work of {h.name} or of third parties who have authorised their use, and are protected by intellectual and industrial property law. Client brands and logos belong to their owners and are shown only as a reference of work done.</p>
    <p class="mt-4">Reproducing, distributing, publicly communicating or transforming the content without prior written permission is not allowed, except where the law permits it.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>4. Liability</h2>
    <p>The owner tries to keep the website available and its information accurate, but does not guarantee that it is free of errors or interruptions, and is not liable for damage caused by misuse of the website or by failures beyond its control. Links to third-party sites (for example social networks or YouTube) are governed by those sites' terms.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>5. Data protection</h2>
    <p>The processing of personal data is explained in the <a href="/en/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>6. Governing law and jurisdiction</h2>
    <p>These terms are governed by Spanish law. Any dispute shall be submitted to the courts that are competent under the law, without prejudice to the rights of consumers.</p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
